Commit 7c874d1 (Require Rex::LibSSH 0.006) raised the pin in cpanfile, but Rex::LibSSH 0.006 is not on CPAN (latest 0.005, no 0.006 tag in rex-libssh), cpanfile.snapshot holds 0.005, and rex-libssh is not in the Makefile VENDOR list. make build therefore fails in cpm install with "Failed to resolve Rex::LibSSH", and so does make test. Fix: add rex-libssh to VENDOR (after its dependencies; its GitHub home is already in SIBLING_HOMES) and adjust t/222, or put the pin back to 0.005 until the release. Found while verifying k453; there it was tested locally with rex-libssh added to the vendor set.

Addendum: Rex::LibSSH 0.006 (HEAD of rex-libssh) in turn requires Net::LibSSH 0.005, which is not on CPAN either (latest 0.004). Both have to go into VENDOR: p5-net-libssh (home Getty/p5-net-libssh, not yet in SIBLING_HOMES), then rex-libssh.

Effect in the test suite: t/222-vendor.t test 5 ('the default list is what cpanfile pins beyond the snapshot') fails as long as cpanfile asks for Rex::LibSSH 0.006 and VENDOR does not list rex-libssh.

